**Design rationale for the "rename pickaxe" milestone:**

The ValidatorAgent correctly identified that `inventory_has` for `iron_pickaxe` alone is pre-satisfied. My solution uses a **two-rule approach**:

1. **`inventory_has` iron_pickaxe min_count 1** — Confirms the player still has the pickaxe (didn't drop or lose it).
2. **`inventory_has` experience_bottle max_count 60** — Confirms the player has thrown at least 4 experience bottles (started with 64, now has ≤60). This is a proxy for "player gained XP levels to use the anvil." Renaming costs 1 level, and each bottle gives 3-11 XP, so the player needs to throw several bottles to reach level 1.

**Why anvil degradation detection is unreliable:** Anvils only have a 12% chance of degrading per use, so checking for `chipped_anvil` at the known position would fail 88% of the time. The experience bottle consumption check is much more reliable as a proxy.

**Note on `max_count` parameter:** If the milestone system doesn't support `max_count` in `inventory_has`, an alternative would be to use `inventory_does_not_have` with `item: experience_bottle, min_count: 61` (i.e., player no longer has 61+ bottles). The MilestoneAgent should confirm which rule parameters are available in the system.

---

